#NEXUS
[Synthetic CC0 time-branch example, NOT a biological inference.
 For time_branch_example, only the root age is supplied: age_mean=100 Ma before present.
 Branch lengths are elapsed time in millions of years, not substitutions.
 Use time branches with the existing age_mean anchor.
 Expected node ages in preorder: 100, 50, 20, 0, 66, 35, 0 Ma.
 These time-unit statements apply only to time_branch_example.
 undated_example is unrooted and has branch lengths with no specified unit.]
BEGIN TREES;
  TRANSLATE
    1 'Fossil taxon A',
    2 'Extant taxon B',
    3 'Fossil taxon C',
    4 'Extant taxon D';
  TREE time_branch_example = [&R]
    ((1[&age_95%HPD={18,22},prob=0.98]:30,
      2:50)
      [&age_95%HPD={42,58},prob=0.96]:50,
     (3:31,
      4:66)
      [&age_95%CredInt={60,72},prob=0.92]:34)
      [&age_mean=100,age_95%HPD={90,110}];
  TREE undated_example = [&U] ((1:0.1,2:0.2):0.3,(3:0.2,4:0.3):0.2);
END;
